Add image generation via the OpenAI Image API

generate_image creates an image from a description and saves it into the
site-assets bucket, recorded in admin_uploads, so the result behaves exactly like
any other asset: list_assets finds it, and it can be used as a blog cover or in a
page edit with no special handling. Shares the OPENAI_API_KEY already present for
voice and research, so no new secret.

On flyers, the tool and the prompt both push back rather than pretending. OpenAI's
own docs state that image models remain weak at precise text placement and
struggle with layout-sensitive compositions, and a flyer is exactly that. A
plausible-looking flyer with a subtly wrong phone number or date is worse than no
flyer, because nobody re-reads a number they did not type. So:
  - generate_image is described as for artwork, backgrounds and photography
  - the prompt instructs the agent to refuse whole-layout requests and offer the
    split that works: generate the artwork, then set the words as real content
  - when a prompt looks text-heavy (flyer, poster, banner, "that says", phone
    number, address), the result carries a warning telling the owner to verify
    every word and number

Also:
- New migration: image_generations, recording prompt, model, size, quality and
  output, since output is not reproducible across settings.
- Failure messages name their own cause: a 403 or verification error tells the
  owner to check API Organization Verification, which is the usual first-run
  blocker for GPT Image models and would otherwise look like a code fault.
- moderation_blocked returns a plain explanation rather than a raw error body.
- Generation timeout is 150s, since complex prompts can take up to two minutes.
- list_image_generations lets the agent reuse an existing image instead of
  generating a near-duplicate.
